<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The vectored airship with hull aerodynamics. Same vehicle as
  airship_vectored_independent, which this merges: only the fluid the hull
  moves through is added, so a run against either model is the same control
  code on two plants.

  Quadratic drag and rotational damping, no added mass. The added-mass terms
  this plugin also accepts are left out on purpose: it applies them as an
  explicit force, and at an airship's ratios (the hull's added sway mass is of
  the order of its dry mass) that diverges within a fraction of a second. Added
  mass belongs in the link's <fluid_added_mass>, which the physics engine folds
  into the spatial inertia, and is not modeled yet.

  The dimensionless coefficients are the airship-control-design reference set
  (c_d 0.08906 axial, c_lat 3.08324 lateral, c_lp_lin 0.04 and c_lp_quad 0.18
  roll, c_mq = c_nr 1.2 pitch and yaw). The reference area and length are this
  hull's, not that design's: this is a 10.5 x 2.5 m hull, so the frontal
  reference radius scales with the half-height to 1.16068 m (A = 4.2323 m^2)
  and the rotational scale is 0.5 * rho * S * L^3 * 0.003438 with S = 66.2984
  m^2 and L = 10.5 m, giving 161.6154 N m. Translational terms are then
  -0.5 * rho * A * c, rotational terms -161.6154 * c.

  The plugin applies its wrench at the link origin (gz::sim::Link has an
  offset form, but Hydrodynamics calls the two-argument AddWorldWrench, which
  the header documents as acting at the origin). That origin is 0.8125 m below
  the centre of mass, while hull drag acts on the hull axis 1.2375 m above it,
  so the moments of the three translational terms come out with the wrong sign
  and 0.66x the size: axial drag pitches the nose down where it should pitch it
  up. At 3 m/s that is 4.3 N m against 579 N m/rad of buoyant pendulum
  stiffness, so it is worth 0.4 deg of trim. The rotational damping, which is
  what a rate loop meets, is a pure couple and is unaffected.
-->
<sdf version="1.10">
  <model name="airship_vectored_independent_aero">
    <include merge="true">
      <uri>model://airship_vectored_independent</uri>
    </include>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-hydrodynamics-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Hydrodynamics">
      <link_name>base_link</link_name>
      <!-- Quadratic drag [N/(m/s)^2] -->
      <xUabsU>-0.2309</xUabsU>
      <yVabsV>-7.9926</yVabsV>
      <zWabsW>-7.9926</zWabsW>
      <!-- Rotational damping [N m/(rad/s)^2], with the linear roll term the
           very lightly damped roll mode needs [N m/(rad/s)] -->
      <kP>-6.4646</kP>
      <kPabsP>-29.0908</kPabsP>
      <mQabsQ>-193.9384</mQabsQ>
      <nRabsR>-193.9384</nRabsR>
      <disable_added_mass>true</disable_added_mass>
    </plugin>
  </model>
</sdf>
